  "methods": {
    "lan": "Native DNS engine using explicit loopback UDP/TCP endpoints 127.0.0.1:5531 and [::1]:5531 against published 0.4.0 Docker images; no system DNS selection. Operator confirmed the client disabled; not independently detected.",
    "internet": "Configured system DNS at the observed 1.1.1.1:53 endpoint; operator confirmed the security intermediary disabled. Recursive observation, not direct authoritative or cache-free proof.",
    "additional_control": "Separate explicit public authoritative endpoint 108.162.192.65:53 for six public additional-data cases; not system DNS. Operator confirmed client disabled; socket destination alone does not exclude interception.",
    "publication": "Set local socket endpoint metadata to null and append a publication note. Preserve all DNS wire bytes, decoded records, timings, remote endpoints and run identity."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Implemented protocol checks are bounded, not full DNS RFC certification or product-baseline approval. Eleven deliberate-fault cases have network_error/inconclusive outcomes in each LAN report; two IPv6-only cases are unavailable in the IPv4 report.",
    "Operator-confirmed-disabled records the supplied acknowledgement, not independent detection of client state or the complete network path.",
    "Optional additional addresses and policy rewrites require scenario interpretation; a reference difference is separate from an RFC finding.",
    "The DNS-behavior recheck ignores all positive TTL differences, generated nonces, timings and other documented volatility. It is not byte identity or an explicit-expectations policy pass.",
    "Old/new catalogue digests differ; the comparison warning remains visible in the published recheck reports."
  ],
